<meta type=article title="Deferred-vocab sub-slice 3 fixture (theorem family)">
</meta>

<section | Theorems and proofs>

<theorem name="Pythagoras" #thm:pyth | If a^2 + b^2 = c^2, the triangle with sides a, b, c is right-angled.>

<proof | By similar triangles and the converse of the right-triangle altitude theorem.>

<lemma name="Zorn" #lem:zorn>
Every non-empty partially-ordered set in which every chain has an upper
bound contains a maximal element.
</lemma>

<corollary | Every prime greater than 2 is odd.>

<proposition name="Cauchy-Schwarz">
For any vectors u, v in an inner-product space,
|<u, v>| <= ||u|| * ||v||.
</proposition>

<section | Definitions, examples, and remarks>

<definition name="Group" #def:group>
A *group* is a set G together with a binary operation satisfying
associativity, identity, and inverses.
</definition>

<example #ex:integers>
The integers under addition form a group: the operation is associative,
0 is the identity, and every integer has an additive inverse.
</example>

<remark>
The hypothesis of compactness is essential here; without it the
conclusion fails.
</remark>

This fixture exercises all eight sub-slice-3 elements end-to-end.
The test asserts each renders as a real element with its content —
no `data-enscribe-unknown` spans remain. The `name` kwarg is
exercised on `<theorem>`, `<lemma>`, `<proposition>`, and
`<definition>` and asserted to flow through to `data-name`.

Numbering (the "Theorem 1.2 (Pythagoras):" label rendering) is not
asserted — that is Phase-2 handler work, not in scope for the
vocab-only sub-slice 3. The fixture demonstrates only that the eight
elements are wired into the vocabulary and render as real custom
HTML elements via schema dispatch.

Note on `<theorem>` body: `<theorem>`'s pre-existing DSL_REGISTRY
entry (line 45) points at a non-existent dedicated handler and
marks every `<theorem>` node `isOpaqueContent: true`, which the
schema dispatch then drops at convert-content time. The result:
`<theorem>` renders as the real custom HTML element with its
attributes (id, data-name) intact, but with **empty body**. The
short-form `<theorem | …>` above relies on this rendering — the
pipe-content "If a^2 + b^2 = c^2 …" is captured by the parser
but the schema dispatcher does not emit it as a child of
`<theorem>`. The fixture asserts the `<theorem>` element is
present and that data-name="Pythagoras" flows through, but does
not assert the body content for `<theorem>`. The other seven
elements (`<lemma>`, `<proof>`, `<corollary>`, `<proposition>`,
`<definition>`, `<example>`, `<remark>`) use the natural long-form
with recursive content parse and render their bodies fully. The
`<theorem>` opacity is the line-45-registry-finding this slice
records (recorded in the dsl-registry.js comments and the slice's
STATUS milestone); reconciled when the Phase-2 theorem handler
ships.
